            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A child stroller apparatus (100) includes a first and a second leg frame (102, 104), a first and a second seat support frame (108, 110), a locking mechanism (140) operable to lock the child stroller apparatus (100) in an unfolded state, an impeding part (178) and an actuating part (182). The first and second seat support frames (108, 110) are pivotally coupled to each other and are respectively coupled pivotally to the first and second leg frame (102, 104), wherein the first seat support frame (108) and the second seat support frame (110) respectively include a seat portion (124) and a side segment (110A) that are pivotally coupled to each other. The locking mechanism (140) includes a latch (144) that is connected with the seat portion (124) and is slidable to an underside of the side segment (110A) for locking the child stroller apparatus (100) in the unfolded state and is slidable away from the underside of the side segment (110A) for folding of the child stroller apparatus (100). The impeding part (178) is connected with the seat portion (124) and is movable between a blocking state and a release state, the impeding part (178) interfering with the locking mechanism (140) in the blocking state to prevent the latch (144) from sliding away from the underside of the side segment (110A), and the impeding part (178) in the release state allowing the latch (144) to slide away from the underside of the side segment (110A). The actuating part (182) is movably assembled with the seat portion (124) and exposed upward for operation through an opening (124C) provided on an upper surface of the seat portion (124), wherein the opening (124C) and the actuating part (182) are disposed at a middle position between a left and a right side edge of the seat portion (124), the actuating part (182) being depressible to urge the impeding part (178) to move from the blocking state to the release state.</p>
            </abstract>
